1
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:38,130
[First Love Again]

2
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:40,960
[Episode 18]

3
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:43,310
What should I do?

4
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,509
-What should...
-Alright.

5
00:01:44,509 --> 00:01:46,970
It's fine.
I'll explain it clearly to my mom.

6
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:50,970
Don't tell your mom.

7
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:54,150
Your mom has already said that
the daughter-in-law she wants

8
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:56,509
must have long hair and a master's degree

9
00:01:56,509 --> 00:01:57,710
and major in finance.

10
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,700
Which part of that sounds like me?

11
00:02:00,310 --> 00:02:01,110
Don't worry.

12
00:02:01,270 --> 00:02:02,990
I can decide who I like.

13
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:06,380
No, no, no.

14
00:02:08,289 --> 00:02:10,630
She asked me to come here
to pump you for information.

15
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:13,900
It would be inappropriate
to contradict myself right now, huh?

16
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:15,570
Stop laughing.

17
00:02:17,770 --> 00:02:19,030
Okay. I won't tell her.

18
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:23,570
Then let's find a suitable time

19
00:02:23,570 --> 00:02:24,500
to tell her.

20
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,840
Do you have time tonight?

21
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:32,860
Yes.

22
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,940
Come to my home
and review the match with me.

23
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:38,820
Are you crazy?

24
00:02:38,850 --> 00:02:40,829
How can I go to your home
when your mom is there?

25
00:02:40,829 --> 00:02:43,560
She's not here tonight.
She's on a business trip.

26
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,880
I can grow my hair long.

27
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:53,740
Short hair looks good.

28
00:03:14,390 --> 00:03:16,920
We've watched enough of it.
Then how about...

29
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,090
we watch a movie?

30
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:19,940
Sure.

31
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:20,720
Okay.

32
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:23,780
Let's watch a horror movie then.

33
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:26,500
People online say that
out of the 100 things couples must do,

34
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:28,760
watching a horror movie is in the top ten.

35
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:32,620
Are you scared?

36
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:34,390
No.

37
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:37,120
It's okay if you're scared. Just say it.

38
00:03:37,829 --> 00:03:38,690
I'm not scared.

39
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:40,350
Here.

40
00:03:40,790 --> 00:03:42,720
Pick a movie. What should we watch?

41
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:44,120
Pick a movie.

42
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:45,980
Then I'll pick one.

43
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,350
Let me choose a...

44
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:49,550
[Ocean's 8] [Swordsman's Romance]

45
00:03:49,579 --> 00:03:51,120
[Folk Legends: The Water Monkeys]
[Song of the Assassins]

46
00:03:51,150 --> 00:03:52,829
This one.

47
00:03:53,390 --> 00:03:55,760
I already wanted to watch this previously.

48
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:57,280
They all say it's good.

49
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,610
Did you fall asleep?

50
00:04:19,190 --> 00:04:19,920
No.

51
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:21,600
My eyes are dry.

52
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:39,470
This...

53
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:42,090
Are your eyes dry again?

54
00:04:42,090 --> 00:04:42,620
No.

55
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:45,810
There's some dirt.

56
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:58,610
Why aren't you even looking at the screen?

57
00:04:59,550 --> 00:05:00,430
I was looking.

58
00:05:01,390 --> 00:05:03,520
I was just afraid
you might be thirsty.

59
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:07,870
You are indeed scared.

60
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:08,730
I'm not scared.

61
00:05:08,750 --> 00:05:09,870
You are just scared.

62
00:05:09,870 --> 00:05:10,430
I'm not scared.

63
00:05:10,430 --> 00:05:11,230
You are obviously scared.

64
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:11,920
I'm not scared!

65
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:16,250
You don't even dare to look at the screen,
and you're saying you're not scared?

66
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,580
Didn't you suggest watching a movie?

67
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:42,670
You two...

68
00:05:42,670 --> 00:05:43,920
A-Auntie.

69
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:47,350
Mom.

70
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,700
Xiangxiang is my girlfriend.

71
00:06:04,670 --> 00:06:05,480
Okay.

72
00:06:10,750 --> 00:06:12,150
This is so embarrassing.

73
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,420
What's embarrassing?

74
00:06:15,230 --> 00:06:16,670
She saw everything.

75
00:06:17,550 --> 00:06:18,550
So what if she did?

76
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:21,790
What's wrong?

77
00:06:21,790 --> 00:06:23,050
I'm just embarrassed.

78
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:26,840
Here. Have some fruits.

79
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:35,120
What's there to be embarrassed about?

80
00:06:35,159 --> 00:06:36,960
You should have told me earlier.

81
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:40,110
If my meeting had not been canceled
at the last minute,

82
00:06:40,110 --> 00:06:42,770
who knows how long
you would have kept it from me?

83
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:44,720
Mom.

84
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:46,190
Actually,

85
00:06:46,670 --> 00:06:48,530
we didn't mean to hide it from you.

86
00:06:49,159 --> 00:06:51,400
I wanted to tell you about it earlier.

87
00:06:51,430 --> 00:06:53,790
But I don't meet any of the standards

88
00:06:54,230 --> 00:06:55,750
you mentioned.

89
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:58,040
I didn't know it was you.

90
00:06:58,550 --> 00:06:59,870
How could those standards

91
00:06:59,870 --> 00:07:01,350
be applied to you?

92
00:07:02,870 --> 00:07:04,990
I've been doing business outside
for so many years,

93
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:06,840
and I know one basic rule,

94
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:09,260
that is, treating each case individually.

95
00:07:10,110 --> 00:07:11,370
Thank you, Auntie Wan.

96
00:07:16,790 --> 00:07:19,320
You have to treat Xiangxiang well
from now on.

97
00:07:20,110 --> 00:07:20,790
I will.

98
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:28,960
Xiangxiang, I have to thank you.

99
00:07:29,670 --> 00:07:30,350
For so many years,

100
00:07:30,350 --> 00:07:32,400
I've never seen him like any girl.

101
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:35,280
I even thought he didn't like girls.

102
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:39,230
Mom.

103
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,640
So you didn't like girls before?

104
00:07:48,990 --> 00:07:50,320
You're still laughing?

105
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:21,770
You're Yu You's boyfriend, right?

106
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:22,920
Yes.

107
00:08:23,190 --> 00:08:25,040
Can you guys stop badgering her?

108
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,870
Just because you said so,

109
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,550
we have to listen to you?

110
00:08:30,350 --> 00:08:31,950
Who do you think you are?

111
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:34,280
Then tell me what you guys want.

112
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:37,059
Are you really willing
to do anything for Yu You?

113
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:42,490
I've ordered all these dishes for you.

114
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,710
After you finish eating them,

115
00:08:45,470 --> 00:08:46,670
we'll talk.

116
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:26,550
Bro.

117
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:29,360
Are you okay?

118
00:09:29,550 --> 00:09:30,520
What happened?

119
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,250
What exactly happened?

120
00:09:37,070 --> 00:09:39,590
He insisted that I should eat all of this.

121
00:09:39,670 --> 00:09:42,400
He even said he'd only talk to me
after I finished.

122
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:46,400
Brother, why are you
making things difficult for him?

123
00:09:48,070 --> 00:09:49,270
What did you call him?

124
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:50,520
Brother.

125
00:09:50,550 --> 00:09:51,310
Your biological brother?

126
00:09:51,310 --> 00:09:52,040
Yes.

127
00:09:54,590 --> 00:09:55,280
Bro...

128
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,420
Bro, I'm sorry.

129
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:02,120
Not bad, brat.

130
00:10:03,950 --> 00:10:04,670
Bro!

131
00:10:05,070 --> 00:10:05,670
Bro!

132
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:07,920
Bro, are you okay?

133
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:16,470
I've been worrying about

134
00:10:16,470 --> 00:10:18,070
how to explain it to your mom.

135
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,710
I didn't expect that what she said

136
00:10:19,710 --> 00:10:21,120
was just talk.

137
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:25,000
Why don't you say
it's because you're special?

138
00:10:26,280 --> 00:10:27,810
What's so special about me?

139
00:10:31,550 --> 00:10:34,070
There are many things
I don't know about my mom.

140
00:10:34,070 --> 00:10:36,400
Nor do I know
what kind of people she likes.

141
00:10:36,670 --> 00:10:37,470
But I think

142
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,700
she seems to like you a lot.

143
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,360
Tonight,
it was all due to your presence here.

144
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:45,190
Otherwise, she and I

145
00:10:45,190 --> 00:10:46,190
couldn't have sat down

146
00:10:46,190 --> 00:10:47,590
to eat and chat together.

147
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:50,170
We usually can't even
say a word to each other.

148
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:56,240
I think

149
00:10:56,470 --> 00:10:59,270
you two just
lack the opportunity to communicate.

150
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:04,290
It's probably because
you're very popular with elders.

151
00:11:08,670 --> 00:11:09,670
I can't help it.

152
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:12,120
Not everyone

153
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:14,590
is as approachable as I am.

154
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:31,470
How are you feeling?

155
00:11:31,670 --> 00:11:32,730
Will you get an upset stomach

156
00:11:32,730 --> 00:11:34,990
that might affect the upcoming matches?

157
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:35,950
I'm fine.

158
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:38,640
I'm really sorry.

159
00:11:38,670 --> 00:11:40,280
I didn't explain
my brother's situation to you clearly,

160
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:42,280
which caused you to misunderstand.

161
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,160
What exactly happened?

162
00:11:44,710 --> 00:11:46,400
The person you competed with
is my brother.

163
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,240
Since I was kid,

164
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,950
whenever a boy appeared around me,

165
00:11:48,950 --> 00:11:50,520
he would ask questions endlessly.

166
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:52,070
I was just annoyed by him following me,

167
00:11:52,070 --> 00:11:53,360
so in a fit of anger,

168
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:55,830
I said you were my boyfriend.

169
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:59,010
I didn't expect
to cause you so much trouble.

170
00:12:01,470 --> 00:12:03,470
Actually, I'm quite happy.

171
00:12:05,830 --> 00:12:06,760
What did you say?

172
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,000
I...

173
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:15,920
I like you.

174
00:12:21,590 --> 00:12:24,120
Actually,
I've been watching your live streams.

175
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,310
After meeting you,

176
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:28,000
I realized you were completely different
from how you were on camera,

177
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,120
so I wanted to truly get to know you.

178
00:12:30,670 --> 00:12:32,730
When they were bullying you on Weibo,

179
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:34,690
I rebutted the comments one by one,

180
00:12:35,830 --> 00:12:38,090
and I found that I could protect you, too.

181
00:12:39,830 --> 00:12:42,000
So, that "Hello" was you?

182
00:12:50,070 --> 00:12:50,710
Well...

183
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,720
Are you willing to accept me?

184
00:13:26,590 --> 00:13:27,400
Han.

185
00:13:27,950 --> 00:13:29,550
I have something to tell you.

186
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:31,280
Okay.

187
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:33,760
Han, how have you been doing

188
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:35,790
with your major courses lately?

189
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:36,520
Not bad.

190
00:13:37,670 --> 00:13:39,760
Later, organize the transcripts

191
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:40,920
for these major courses,

192
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:42,040
and send me a copy.

193
00:13:42,670 --> 00:13:44,360
Why do you need the transcripts?

194
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:47,420
I just want to know more about
your studying in general.

195
00:13:47,470 --> 00:13:48,760
From now on,

196
00:13:49,470 --> 00:13:52,000
you need to focus on your major courses.

197
00:13:52,550 --> 00:13:54,550
Just play fewer basketball games.

198
00:14:04,670 --> 00:14:05,430
Look.

199
00:14:05,790 --> 00:14:06,950
These are the admission requirements

200
00:14:06,950 --> 00:14:08,240
for several
top business administration schools

201
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,470
in Canada.

202
00:14:09,590 --> 00:14:10,710
Take a look later.

203
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,310
There's the University of Toronto

204
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:13,510
and York University.

205
00:14:13,950 --> 00:14:15,610
Why are you showing this to me?

206
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:18,210
You'll be in your senior year soon.

207
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,760
This is a very crucial time

208
00:14:19,760 --> 00:14:21,430
for your future prospects.

209
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:24,240
I've been considering the direction
of your future development.

210
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:25,430
I've also talked with

211
00:14:25,430 --> 00:14:26,790
my partners in Canada.

212
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:28,950
If all the conditions are suitable,

213
00:14:28,950 --> 00:14:29,880
after you graduate,

214
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:31,760
going to Canada for postgraduate studies

215
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:32,520
would be a great choice.

216
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:33,280
And then,

217
00:14:34,670 --> 00:14:37,400
you want me to manage the company
with you, right?

218
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:39,340
I know what you want to say.

219
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:41,130
But this is not what I want.

220
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:44,470
When you got into Jiangcheng University,

221
00:14:44,470 --> 00:14:46,670
I shouldn't have let you
join the basketball team.

222
00:14:46,670 --> 00:14:48,000
But I also did as you said

223
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:50,280
and applied for the major
of business administration.

224
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,310
When you were a kid,
I supported you playing basketball,

225
00:14:52,310 --> 00:14:54,070
as I wanted you to treat it as a hobby.

226
00:14:54,070 --> 00:14:56,930
Do you really think
you could make a living out of it?

227
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:58,310
How many college students

228
00:14:58,310 --> 00:15:00,760
can actually
make it to the professional league?

229
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:02,640
Fine. Even if you could do so,

230
00:15:02,670 --> 00:15:04,120
being unable to become a key player,

231
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,720
how much salary can you earn?

232
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,310
You'll also have to face injuries

233
00:15:07,310 --> 00:15:09,770
and risks
like the team's operating status.

234
00:15:11,470 --> 00:15:12,710
When I get old in the future,

235
00:15:12,710 --> 00:15:16,110
can I still support you financially
for the rest of your life?

236
00:15:16,430 --> 00:15:17,830
Think about it carefully.

237
00:15:17,830 --> 00:15:19,280
Between playing basketball
and your future,

238
00:15:19,280 --> 00:15:20,360
which is more important?

239
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,890
You're the most important!

240
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:25,670
Since childhood,

241
00:15:25,670 --> 00:15:28,040
has there ever been anything
I could decide for myself?

242
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:29,400
When I was a kid,
and we moved to Jiangcheng,

243
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:30,590
didn't I only find out about it
at the last minute

244
00:15:30,590 --> 00:15:32,710
when you had already packed the luggage?

245
00:15:32,710 --> 00:15:34,360
Later, you insisted on divorcing my dad.

246
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:35,420
I didn't want that.

247
00:15:35,830 --> 00:15:37,470
Yes, you two were getting divorced,

248
00:15:37,470 --> 00:15:38,880
and I couldn't make the decision for you.

249
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:40,190
But what happened next?

250
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:41,920
You insisted on living with me.

251
00:15:42,310 --> 00:15:44,760
But how many days have you actually
been at home these past few years?

252
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:46,420
-Do you know what I want?
-I...

253
00:15:48,070 --> 00:15:49,760
You only care about yourself.

254
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:07,640
Captain.

255
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:09,590
That's enough. Take a break.

256
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,000
Stop practicing.

257
00:16:16,190 --> 00:16:17,240
Stop practicing.

258
00:16:26,070 --> 00:16:27,670
Have you made him angry again?

259
00:16:27,670 --> 00:16:28,790
He's acting as if he were possessed today.

260
00:16:28,790 --> 00:16:31,120
Time's up, but he still keeps practicing.

261
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:37,790
Gu Han, stop practicing! Take a break!

262
00:16:37,050 --> 00:16:38,190
[Private Training Area] [No Entry
for Non-Private Training Members]

263
00:16:41,670 --> 00:16:42,600
I'm out of ideas.

264
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,960
What are you thinking about?

265
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:45,140
Thinking about the title of my paper.

266
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:56,360
You're lying.

267
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,990
You've been like this
since this afternoon.

268
00:18:01,990 --> 00:18:04,050
What are you thinking about exactly?

269
00:18:15,190 --> 00:18:15,880
My mom.

270
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:34,920
Your mom did it for your own good.

271
00:18:36,670 --> 00:18:39,600
She doesn't understand
why I like basketball at all.

272
00:18:40,230 --> 00:18:42,290
Has she ever watched you play a match?

273
00:18:43,750 --> 00:18:44,640
Never.

274
00:18:47,270 --> 00:18:48,320
Well...

275
00:18:50,710 --> 00:18:52,270
Next time, when you have a match,

276
00:18:52,270 --> 00:18:54,070
could you invite her to watch it?

277
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:55,160
Why?

278
00:18:55,750 --> 00:18:56,800
Because I think

279
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:59,240
your problem is the lack of communication.

280
